. This PR switches it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` so the code does what the docstring and test expect.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-round-half-even", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **The bug:** in `src/money.py`, `round_money` said in its comment that it used banker's rounding (FIN-212), but the code actually rounded halves up. So `2.665` became `2.68` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **The fix:** branch `fix/round-half-even`, commit `08d3cd5986`. It's a one-line change to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, so the code now does what the comment says.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID. The fix is based on the test and the code comment, which both call for banker's rounding.\n\nThe PR hasn't been merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}